comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T20:23:47.453Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against core SDK actionability declarations and sibling README contracts: core collectBlockedByIds/resolveItemBlockers/computeActionabilityReport decide readiness; gantt resources allocates owner capacity; pm-swarm resources owns fenced reservations; observed-duration calibration includes waits but does not declare them. This feature adds read-only explicit elapsed wait bounds, with no reservation, reminder, ownership or scheduling mutation. CLI registry version verified as 2026.10.28; retained repository development pin 2026.10.25. Plan: one boundary schema, SDK status roles and ordering kernel, bounded TOON/JSON, seeded native-state preservation, public archive validation and CI npm/Bun gates."
  "2026-10-28T20:32:37.281Z",codex-agent,"Implemented effortWaitingPreview and previewEffortWaiting plus gantt waiting. ONE shared strict duration schema covers dense inputs and finite bounded outputs; SDK runtime roles classify custom statuses, the SDK execution kernel handles ordering, and the supported active host supplies the fresh certified corpus. No import, sync, apply, journal, lease or shared write state is added. Focused validation: 500 seeded native-operation/replay sequences passed, 500 random custom registries passed, packed TOON/JSON no-git preview preserved a real claim and native SDK state. Public archive at 9d307c26e4956a5fa43c84546bb886e3cf58c7a9: 119 corpus, 9 nonterminal, 2 declared hypothetical waits, 6 missing effort, 540 known effort minutes, 7 unknown completions, 3 returned rows, 1250 JSON bytes; two previews took 7357 ms on the loaded host. SDK read-back and durable hashes unchanged. Behavioral reverts in a disposable copy each failed: ignored wait, zero substituted for unknown upper bound, status-name terminal classification. All three restored checks passed. Full release gates will run in CI under npm and Bun; local work stays focused with at most two test workers."
  "2026-10-28T20:36:24.337Z",codex-agent,"Final input review: native ids, declared wait keys, graph rows and dependency targets normalize through SDK normalizeRawItemId before comparisons, with canonical collisions refused. The focused new module measured 100% lines, branches and functions. Public-archive utility is shared with the existing resource validator to keep the unchanged zero-duplication gate. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint and docstring checks pass; full npm/Bun release gates and five packed-install scenarios remain assigned to CI. The preview is a continuous-minute lower-bound model, not owner/calendar allocation; unknown native estimates remain unknown."
  "2026-10-28T20:38:20.583Z",codex-agent,"Linked verification completed: pm test --run --progress executed node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/waiting.test.ts, 7 passed / 0 failed, including all 500 seeded state sequences and packed no-git ownership checks. Project test-result tracking is disabled, so this comment preserves the measured result without changing project policy. Final normalization-specific focused subset: 5 passed / 0 failed. Repeated public archive validation on the final implementation kept the same 119/9/540/6/7 counts and 1250-byte JSON; two previews took 2228 ms. Revert proof repeated successfully after the final normalization changes. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification; claim released before the final CI head. Full CI evidence will be attached to the PR without changing the tested commit."
  "2026-10-28T20:40:09.291Z",codex-agent,"Pre-push health: repository settings, integrity and history drift checks pass. The normal local host reports only a gate-failing global pm-github host-version skew (development SDK 2026.10.25 versus global extension host 2026.10.28); an isolated HOME with system/global git config disabled passes strict health including required clone-local drivers. Existing historical-provenance and pending-telemetry advisories remain outside scope; no history or telemetry settings were changed. All public added lines passed a privacy scan. No new core CLI/SDK defect was established."
  "2026-10-28T21:00:38.124Z",codex-agent,"First CI run 40765477075 measured 384 tests: 381 passed and 3 failed on both Node versions. Root causes: changing the established workspace graph client to the active extension facade hid custom relationship contracts, and the exact preflight-scope test needed the new command. Restored the existing workspace SDK graph adapter, updated the owned command contract, and added valid/refused source-harness executions of gantt waiting (packed execution alone does not cover the source handler). New waiting module itself measured 100% lines/branches/functions in both CI jobs. No SDK gap is claimed. Focused regression verification and a fresh exact-head CI run follow."
  "2026-10-28T21:02:48.149Z",codex-agent,"Post-CI correction: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=packed\\ command test/waiting.test.ts passed 1/1, exercising successful and refused source handlers as well as the packed CLI and SDK; npm run lint and npm run duplication pass (0% duplicates). The existing registry-ordering/smoke regression suite is running against the restored workspace adapter. A fresh exact-head CI run is required; the first run remains explicit failed evidence, not a release-gate pass."
  "2026-10-28T21:06:14.467Z",codex-agent,"Correction verification passed: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/registry-ordering.test.ts test/smoke.test.ts => 16 passed, 0 failed, including installed/source custom ordering and seven real predecessor traversals with four-way overlap. Updated waiting packed/source test => 1 passed, 0 failed. Build, test typecheck, lint and unchanged zero-duplication gate pass. The initial CI failure is preserved at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart/actions/runs/40765477075 (381/384 on both Node versions). A fresh CI run for the correction commit is pending; use PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart/pull/197 for its exact run URL and final npm/Bun gate counts. Every new source/pm push requires fresh exact-head evidence; no full-gate success is claimed from the superseded run."
